course: dictionary
lesson: 11778
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Beaten is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context and they give you clues. Then try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: «We were beaten 3–0 by the other school.» Here beaten means lost to them in a game. «The traveller was beaten by robbers.» Here beaten means hit many times. The words game and robbers are the clues.
explain: In a recipe, «Add two beaten eggs to the flour» means the eggs have been mixed hard with a fork or whisk. A path can also be beaten: «a beaten path» is flat and hard because many feet have walked on it.
fact: Beaten is the form of beat that you use after have or be, as in «have beaten» or «was beaten».
fact: «Beaten» can mean lost to someone in a game.
fact: «Beaten» can mean hit many times.
fact: «Beaten eggs» means eggs mixed hard with a fork or whisk.
fact: «Off the beaten track» means in a quiet, faraway place, and «can't be beaten» means the best.
exercise: «We were beaten 3–0 by the other school.» What does beaten mean? | Hit many times | *Lost to them in a game | Mixed hard with a whisk | Flattened by many feet
exercise: «The traveller was beaten by robbers.» What does beaten mean here? | Made smooth and flat | Mixed with a fork | *Hit many times | Lost a game
exercise: «Add two beaten eggs to the flour.» What does beaten mean in this recipe? | Tired and worn out | *Mixed hard with a fork or whisk | Hit many times | Lost to someone
test: «The village was off the beaten track, far from the main road.» What does off the beaten track mean? | Sitting on the track to win a race | Easy to find on a map | Full of beaten cars | *In a quiet, faraway place
test: Mia says, «Our team can't be beaten!» What does she mean? | *They are the best | They always lose | They have been hit many times | They are very tired
exam: «After the long race, Sam felt tired and beaten.» What does beaten mean here? | *Tired and defeated | Hit by a ball | Flattened into a path | Mixed with a whisk
